If we choose this direction, anyone using the offline mode to update will lose data, whereas we can use raw SQL to process the data conversion from bytes to JSON. 

```
DO $$
DECLARE
    batch_size INT := 2; 
    offset INT := 0;
    rows_affected := 0;
BEGIN
    LOOP
        UPDATE dag_run
        SET conf_json = CONVERT_FROM(conf, 'UTF8')::JSONB
        WHERE id IN (
            SELECT id
            FROM dag_run
            WHERE conf_json IS NULL 
            ORDER BY id
            LIMIT batch_size
            OFFSET offset
        )
        RETURNING 1 INTO rows_affected;
        IF NOT FOUND THEN
            EXIT;
        END IF;
        offset := offset + batch_size;
    END LOOP;
END $$;
```
This is rough but might work for postgresql
